changes.body:
Adds a once decorator to funcutils that ensures a zero-argument function executes exactly once, caching the result for all subsequent calls.
Thread-safe via threading.RLock + functools.cache — concurrent callers block until the first execution completes, then all receive the cached result. Guaranteed single execution even under contention.
Usage
from boltons.funcutils import once
@once
def load_config():
    return parse_config_from_disk()
Changes
- boltons/funcutils.py: Added once decorator with docstring and doctest
- tests/test_funcutils.py: Added tests for single execution, identity of cached result, and thread safety under concurrent access

